     $$P = \mathcal{V}(k, u, v) = u V_1 + v V_2 + (1 - u - v) V_3$$
-    Calculate the interpolated normal $n$:
+2.  Compute the interpolated normal $n$ using per-vertex normals $n_1, n_2, n_3$:
